  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Train Kept A-Rollin' Jam** (1 other source): Session tape dated 26 March 1975 with guests; John Cipollina may be playing in the jam [1]\n- **Blues Groove, take 3** (1 other source): The end of this take features a duet between Otis and Jerry [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Stronger Than Dirt**: rare: 10 archived performances [3]\n- **Disco Slipknot, take 1**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Disco Slipknot, take 2**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Disco Slipknot, take 3**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Train Kept A-Rollin' Jam**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Low Down Payment**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Hideaway**: rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Blues Groove, take 1**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1975-03-12.163701.studio-sampler.brown.flac1648** (recommended): soundboard; 14 songs; 80 min [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1975-03-12.163701.studio-sampler.brown.flac1648**: taped by This is a sampler from cassettes made by Steve Brown for Jerry Garcia to listen to after the sessions.; source: Soundboard > Cassette > DVD > WAV > FLAC [1]",
